--- live-original-normalized/MACOS.md	1969-12-31 19:00:00
+++ live-copy-safety-normalized/MACOS.md	2026-08-31 10:24:26
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# macOS bring-up notes
+
+Build a dependency-only overlay, then run the fleet with Apple system tools. The overlay contains
+links to `gh` and `python3` only; it does not expose Homebrew GNU coreutils:
+
+```bash
+fleet_tool_dir=$(/usr/bin/mktemp -d /tmp/fleet-macos-tools.XXXXXX)
+gh_path=$(command -v gh)
+python3_path=$(command -v python3)
+/bin/ln -s "$gh_path" "$fleet_tool_dir/gh"
+/bin/ln -s "$python3_path" "$fleet_tool_dir/python3"
+env PATH="$fleet_tool_dir:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin" \
+  MAI_TAI_REPO=/Users/velkris/Projects/project-mai-tai \
+  /bin/bash ./selftest.sh
+```
+
+The compatibility helpers also accept fail-closed absolute overrides when an exact implementation
+must be selected: `FLEET_SHA256SUM`, `FLEET_SHASUM`, `FLEET_MD5SUM`, `FLEET_MD5`,
+`FLEET_BSD_STAT`, `FLEET_GNU_STAT`, `FLEET_BSD_DATE`, `FLEET_GNU_DATE`, and `FLEET_PYTHON`.
+
+If a fresh copy from Windows lands the shell scripts with CRLF line endings, normalize first.
+Darwin rejects a CRLF shebang before any in-script guard runs, while Windows Git Bash may execute
+it; Windows therefore proves CR-byte presence before running the same normalization:
+
+```bash
+/usr/bin/perl -pi -e 's/\r$//' ./*.sh ./fleet.cmd
+chmod +x ./*.sh
+```
+
+This normalization is external on purpose. A script with a CRLF shebang cannot repair itself before
+Darwin tries to parse it. `selftest.sh` creates a fresh CRLF copy; Darwin proves direct execution
+initially fails, while Windows Git Bash proves raw CR bytes are present. Both then apply these exact
+commands, verify every shell script is LF, and prove direct shebang execution succeeds.
